{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkxz8VhxvPGGS81Z6sLo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'd go with option 1. Fairly sure. It opens straight on \"עוקב מדד s&p 500\", the S&P thing my friends talk about, with every company in one list. I can see the cheapest at the top without doing any work: מנורה מבטחים \"0.52%\" החיסכון, \"13.79%\" over 3 years. I know Menora, I've seen their ads.\n\n**How it went:**\n- **Top of the page.** Read the heading \"כל המסלולים בכל החברות\". Saw three option buttons, and the third one had a \"מומלץ\" tag. There was also a \"מחשב / טלפון\" toggle. I'm on my phone, so I wondered why I'm seeing the computer version.\n- **Option 1.** The product chip \"קופת גמל להשקעה 143\" was already on. That name sounds like a pension thing for old people, but there's a \"מה זה קופת גמל להשקעה\" link. I didn't tap it. Then the S&P block: rows of companies, two fees each (\"החיסכון\", \"ההפקדות\"), a ring chart, \"מניות\" and \"מט\"ח\" percentages, and the return. Rows at the bottom like אינפיניטי, ילין לפידות and איילון had \"פחות מ־3 שנים\" instead of a number, so I ignored them. I skipped the grey text under the table.\n- **Option 2.** Same top again, then a block per company. Harel came first, with 16 tracks: מניות, כללי, הלכה, אשראי ואג\"ח and so on. I don't care about most of them. It's a very long scroll before I'd even reach the next company, and I got bored around Mor.\n- **Option 3, the \"מומלץ\" one.** It's a big grid of brown-orange boxes, all percentages between 0.50% and 0.73%. It all looks the same to me and nothing pops. I didn't get what the darker or lighter colour means, and I didn't read the line that explains it. My guess is darker means cheaper. Under the grid it repeats option 1's S&P list anyway. I would have closed the page at the grid.\n\n**Words I didn't get:** \"מט\"ח\", \"חשיפה\", \"קופה\" with numbers like \"13874\", \"ההפקדות\" next to \"החיסכון\" (two